- description: Queries ABOM runs against ABOM's own workflows

# Narrower than abom-findings.qls on purpose. This suite is a gate on one repository at review
# time, not the attribution corpus: a finding here has to be worth blocking a pull request
# for, so the experimental queries that abom-findings.qls keeps are absent.
- import: codeql-suites/actions-security-and-quality.qls
  from: codeql/actions-queries
  version: 0.6.38

# Retains `Debug/SyntaxError` and `Diagnostics/SuccessfullyExtractedFiles`, which the upstream
# suite includes and which report nothing about security. They stay because a self audit that
# cannot distinguish "no findings" from "nothing was extracted" is worse than no self audit.

# `actions/unpinned-tag` is excluded and `ActionsLockAware/UncoveredActionRef.ql` takes the place
# it held. The rule asks whether a ref is a full-length SHA. This repository's pin is
# `.github/workflows/actions.lock`: the ref is the key, the lock records the commit the runner
# executes, and a `uses:` the lock does not account for is refused before any job starts. Satisfying
# the rule again would mean inline SHAs, which is the bare-SHA key `gh actions-lock` warns about and
# `make pins` would report -- the two checks now pull opposite ways, and only one of them describes
# what is enforced.
- exclude:
    id: actions/unpinned-tag

# Coverage is also the stricter question, which is why this is a replacement and not a removal.
# `unpinned-tag` exempts the `actions` and `github` owners outright and accepts any bare SHA, so it
# examined 2 of this repository's 10 references. Coverage examines every one of them, and reports a
# SHA no lock entry resolves -- the case a pinning rule reads as its best outcome.
#
# Upgrading is not the fix. `actions-queries` 0.6.36 makes `unpinned-tag` lock-aware and stops it
# reporting `$/`, but the latest published version is 0.6.35, and even 0.6.36 keeps both exemptions.
- query: ActionsLockAware/UncoveredActionRef.ql
  from: advanced-security/abom-actions-findings-src

# What the lockfile's absence would mean here. This repository keeps a lock, so this is silent --
# and it fires if that ever stops being true, including if a toolchain change stops the lockfile
# reaching the database, which would otherwise read as a clean gate.
- query: ActionsLockAware/ActionsLockMissingForWorkflow.ql
  from: advanced-security/abom-actions-findings-src
